{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Nose-ring.</b> There is a נזם that is on the nose and also on the ear, and that on the nose hung from a cord tied to the forehead." "<b>Beka.</b> Half a shekel, from the root of נבקע (split)." "<b>And bracelets.</b> From the form of צמיד פתיל (Numbers 19:15), for upon one hand the one צמיד is two, and its form is known."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:36.079607288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}